title: What else do people rest on?
type: text/vnd.tiddlywiki

People rest, repose, lean, and lay on things. A chair is one way.

Kramer, on Seinfeld, wants levels all over his apartment. Levels are seating, and they do other jobs too.

Some ergonomic studies say a lecture hall works better without seats: tiered platforms people can sit on in different ways, lie on, or reach with other mobility devices.

What is a chair for?

